pan="1">65.9 (166)</td></tr><tr><td align="left" colspan="4" rowspan="1">Bothers you if your child becomes a smoker<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn4-ijerph-06-00433">**</xref></td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x02003;<italic>Yes</italic></td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">32.5 (160)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">67.5 (333)</td><td align="center" rowspan="2" colspan="1">0.124</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x02003;<italic>No</italic></td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">26.0 (44)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">74.0 (125)</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="tfn3-ijerph-06-00433"><label>*</label><p>Student t-test, equal variances assumed, results depicted as mean&#x000b1;standard deviation</p></fn><fn id="tfn4-ijerph-06-00433"><label>**</label><p>Chi-squared test, exact, two sided, presented as % (n)</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="t3-ijerph-06-00433" position="float"><label>Table 3.</label><caption><p>Adjusted Odds Ratio of the paternal characteristics that were found to be significantly associated with childhood exposure to SHS due to parental smoking<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn5-ijerph-06-00433">*</xref>.</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" rowspan="2" colspan="1"/><th align="center" rowspan="2" colspan="1">B coefficient</th><th align="center" rowspan="2" colspan="1">O.R</th><th align="center" colspan="2" rowspan="1">95% C.I.</th><th align="center" rowspan="2" colspan="1">p-value</th></tr><tr><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Lower</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Upper</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" colspan="6" rowspan="1"><bold>Paternal smoking in the house in front of the children<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn6-ijerph-06-00433">**</xref></bold></td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Paternal Educational st